artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $S^{2m+1}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2m+2}$ be the unit sphere of odd dimension $2m+1$, $m\ge 1$, with its standard round metric. A unit vector field $V$ on $S^{2m+1}$ has volume
$$\mathrm{vol}(V)=\int_{S^{2m+1}}\sqrt{\det(I+(\nabla V)^{t}\nabla V)}\,d\mathrm{vol},$$
where $\nabla$ is the Levi-Civita connection. A Hopf vector field $H$ on $S^{2m+1}$ is a unit Killing vector field tangent to the fibers of a Hopf fibration; equivalently, $H_p=Jp$ for a complex structure $J$ on $\mathbb{R}^{2m+2}$ compatible with the inner product.

Fix an integer $r$ with $1\le r\le m$ (so that, after a unitary change of coordinates, one may split $\mathbb{R}^{2m+2}=\mathbb{C}^{r+1}\oplus\mathbb{C}^{m-r}$). Consider a smooth one-parameter family $\{V_t\}_{t\in[0,1]}$ of unit vector fields on $S^{2m+1}$ such that:
\begin{itemize}
\item $V_0=H$ is a Hopf vector field;
\item $V_1$ is a parallel-transport unit vector field on $S^{2m+1}$ (a unit vector field obtained by parallel translation along great circles from a fixed point, defined on the complement of the antipode and continuously extended);
\item the family interpolates between $V_0$ and $V_1$ in the standard way associated with the index $r$, so that the volume function $t\mapsto \mathrm{vol}(V_t)$ satisfies $\frac{d}{dt}\mathrm{vol}(V_t)\big|_{t=0^+}<0$ (volume decreases for small $t>0$).
\end{itemize}

Determine all pairs $(m,r)$ with $m\ge 1$, $1\le r\le m$, for which the function $t\mapsto\mathrm{vol}(V_t)$ is strictly decreasing on the entire interval $[0,1]$ (not merely for small $t>0$).

